            <ArticleTitle>The Effects of Maternal Obesity on Neonates, Infants, Children, Adolescents, and Adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>216-27</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/GRF.0000000000000179</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With the increasing prevalence of obesity, including among women of childbearing age, there is increasing concern regarding the short-term and long-term effects on the offspring of women who are overweight and obese. In this paper we report the results of our review of the recent literature suggesting important adverse short-term and long-term consequences of maternal obesity on their children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
